# Linux for Security — Minimal Reference

## Navigation & Files
| Cmd | Use |
|---|---|
| `pwd` / `ls` / `cd` | location, list, move |
| `touch` / `mkdir` / `cp` / `mv` / `rm` | create, copy, move, delete |
| `cat` / `less` / `head` / `tail` | read files (full / paged / start / end) |

## Search
| Cmd | Use |
|---|---|
| `grep "pattern" file` | search **text** |
| `find . -name "file"` | search **filesystem** |

## Permissions
```
-rwxr-xr--   owner|group|others   r=4 w=2 x=1
```
| Octal | Perm |
|---|---|
| 755 | rwx r-x r-x |
| 644 | rw- r-- r-- |

- `chmod 755 file` → permissions
- `chown user:group file` → ownership

## Users & Privileges
- `whoami` — current user
- `id` — UID/GID/groups
- `sudo <cmd>` — elevated exec

## Processes & Jobs
| Cmd | Use |
|---|---|
| `ps aux` / `top` / `htop` | list / monitor processes |
| `kill <pid>` / `kill -9 <pid>` | graceful / force term (avoid -9 by default) |
| `cmd &` / `jobs` / `fg` / `Ctrl+Z` | background, list, foreground, suspend |

## Pipes & Redirection
- `>` overwrite, `>>` append, `\|` pipe (stdout → stdin)
- Recon pattern: `ps aux | grep nginx`

## Text Processing (recon/log parsing)
`sort` · `uniq` · `wc -l` · `cut` · `awk` · `sed`
→ `sort file | uniq` = dedupe after sort

## Shell & Environment
| Cmd | Use |
|---|---|
| `export VAR=val` | persist var to child procs |
| `echo $PATH` | executable search dirs |
| `which <bin>` | resolve which binary runs |

## Networking
| Cmd | Use |
|---|---|
| `ip addr` / `ip route` | interfaces / routing |
| `ping <host>` | reachability (ICMP) |
| `curl -I` / `curl -v` | headers only / verbose — inspect & manipulate HTTP |
| `wget <url>` | download |
| `ss -tuln` | listening sockets (t=TCP u=UDP l=listening n=numeric) |

## SSH
- `ssh user@host` — remote login
- `scp` — secure file copy over SSH *(needs more practice)*

## Package Mgmt (Debian)
`apt update` (refresh lists) → `apt upgrade` (upgrade installed) → `apt install/remove <pkg>`

## Services (systemd)
- `systemctl status/start/stop/restart <svc>`
- `systemctl enable <svc>` = boot startup (≠ `start` = now)

## Logs
- `journalctl -u <svc> -f` — follow service logs
- `dmesg` — kernel ring buffer (hw/kernel events)

## Bash Scripting
```bash
#!/bin/bash
if [ -f "file.txt" ]; then echo "exists"; else echo "missing"; fi
for f in *.txt; do echo "$f"; done
while true; do echo "running"; done
```
`chmod +x script.sh && ./script.sh`

